From: Juan Sanchez <juanesf91@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: sunxi: sram: allow RES1_CTRL (0x168) in the A733 regmap

The A733 system-control regmap is exposed by sunxi_sram and restricted
by sunxi_sram_regmap_accessible_reg(). Its variant sets has_hdmi_rescal,
which allows RESCAL_CTRL (0x160) and RES0_CTRL (0x164), but not
RES1_CTRL (0x168) - and max_register stops at 0x164.

The USB2 PHY of the DWC3 (U2P0) needs to clear the RES200 trim in
RES1_CTRL during its 200 ohm calibration; going through the regmap
currently returns -EIO and phy_init() aborts before touching the PHY,
which makes the DWC3 probe fail with "failed to initialize core".
A second ioremap of the same 0x03000000 range is not an option either,
because sunxi_sram already owns that mem region (-EBUSY).

Add RES1_CTRL to the whitelist (and raise max_register) for variants
with has_hdmi_rescal. It is the third register of the same RESCAL
block, so this does not widen access to any unrelated hardware.

Signed-off-by: Juan Sanchez <juanesf91@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sunxi_sram.c
@@ -368,6 +368,7 @@
 #define SUNXI_SYS_LDO_CTRL_REG		0x150
 #define SUNXI_SYS_RESCAL_CTRL_REG	0x160
 #define SUNXI_SYS_RES0_CTRL_REG		0x164
+#define SUNXI_SYS_RES1_CTRL_REG		0x168
 
 static bool sunxi_sram_regmap_accessible_reg(struct device *dev,
 					     unsigned int reg)
@@ -382,7 +383,8 @@
 	if (reg == SUNXI_SYS_LDO_CTRL_REG && variant->has_ldo_ctrl)
 		return true;
 	if ((reg == SUNXI_SYS_RESCAL_CTRL_REG ||
-	     reg == SUNXI_SYS_RES0_CTRL_REG) && variant->has_hdmi_rescal)
+	     reg == SUNXI_SYS_RES0_CTRL_REG ||
+	     reg == SUNXI_SYS_RES1_CTRL_REG) && variant->has_hdmi_rescal)
 		return true;
 
 	return false;
@@ -407,7 +409,7 @@
 	.val_bits       = 32,
 	.reg_stride     = 4,
 	/* last defined register */
-	.max_register   = SUNXI_SYS_RES0_CTRL_REG,
+	.max_register   = SUNXI_SYS_RES1_CTRL_REG,
 	/* other devices have no business accessing other registers */
 	.readable_reg	= sunxi_sram_regmap_accessible_reg,
 	.writeable_reg	= sunxi_sram_regmap_accessible_reg,
